I've not read this group for a while, so this may be old hat..

The / cursor (identify) sequence could stand some further improvement:
instead of requiring '.' why not just identify the object/creature
beneath the cursor & do away with all those -more-'s. Just press Esc
to quit is sufficient. (Yes it IS better than it was, thanks!)
In this particular area, any key should be valid for -more-. Can you
use ungetc() to pass the character to the cursor handler if -more- has
to stay?

The present 3.0 code has a helpful bug in it at the moment:
if you press '.' while on an UNMAPPED square, it'll still tell you if it's
a floor, corridor or door. It quits only if its bedrock or there's an object
on it. Considering this takes NO moves, it's quite handy when trying to
decide whether or not to zap a wand down a corridor when there's a risk it'll
bounce back at you if the corridor's short.

